    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not about talking, though. talking just makes it real. and every time i speak, it just reminds me that i'm a shell of what i used to be. i look at my old photos, my old work, and i just feel this overwhelming sense of... finality. like the verdict is already in. the world has already decided who i am and what i'm worth, and it's not anything good. how do you even keep going when you're just waiting for the next wave of hate to hit? it's like i'm already gone, i'm just stuck in this body for no reason.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
